Since the infusion rate is 0.5 mg/kg/min, we can convert the infusion time to minutes:

706 mg/min * (1 kg / 17.65 kg) = 39.3 minutes

So, the loading dose of phenytoin should be administered to the child for $\boxed{39.3}$ minutes.
