3. Evaluating the effectiveness of interventions: Epidemiologists play a crucial role in evaluating the effectiveness of health interventions. This can be done by comparing the health outcomes of people who took in the intervention with those who not. This data helps determine the success of the intervention and its impact on the health of the community.

