","The bond between nitrogen and oxygen in the molecule NO2 (nitrogen dioxide) is polar. This is because nitrogen and oxygen have different electronegativities, which means they do not share the shared electrons equally in the bond. Oxygen is more electronegative than nitrogen, so the electrons in the bond are pulled more towards the oxygen atom. This creates a partial negative charge on the oxygen atom and a partial positive charge on the nitrogen atom, making the bond polar.
