","Marfan’s syndrome is caused by genetic mutations in the gene encoding the **tropticin-1 (TP1) gene**, also known as the **Trr1 gene**. This gene encodes the transcription factor **Trr1**, which is responsible for producing the **tropellin-1 protein**, a critical component of the **actin-tropellin-actin trimers** (TAPs). TAPs are essential for the proper functioning of the **actin-tropellin receptor (Trr1)**, which is involved in the regulation of the renin-angiotensin axis and the renin-angiotensin-angiotensin-1 (RAa) axis. Additionally, the Trr1 protein is involved in the regulation of the renin-angiotensin-angiotensin-1 (RAa) axis, which is essential for the regulation of blood pressure and fluid balance.
